xudo (beta): every privileged request asks for a password. There is no
agent path in this release. Agent detection is not a security boundary.
Read SECURITY.md at /usr/share/doc/xudo/SECURITY.md and at
https://github.com/YaminT/xudo/blob/main/SECURITY.md.
The xudo group is empty by design,
so `xudo exec` is refused until you run `sudo usermod -aG xudo <you>` and
log in again; `xudo doctor --fix` proposes the same change. Without systemd
(journald), every privileged request is refused.
